The system comprises the following:
1) House gravity connection;
2) Collection chamber with interface unit;
3) Vacuum connection and piping;
4) Vacuum station; and
5) Odour fitter and ring main. One of the characteristic features of this system is the presence of the collection chamber. The collection chamber serves or reserve storage for a day, during any power failure. Sewage flows by gravity into a collection chamber and remains for a short time with reserve storage availability. When the level rises, a starter valve activates the vacuum piston valve to open and to allow the sewage water with air to be derived in the vacuum network. Multiple connections can be linked to a single collection chamber. The system can be used in the following applications:
i) Septic tank replacements;
ii) Ribbon development and new residential layouts;
iii) Villages;
iv) Industrial areas;
v) Islands;
